        "title": "2. Neuter nouns with an -εσ- stem",
        "practiceTopic": "es-nouns",
        "body": [
          "In nouns such as τὸ γένος, the sigma between vowels disappears and the neighboring vowels contract: γένεσ-ος becomes γένους. The nominative and accusative singular end in -ος; this does not make the noun masculine or second declension.",
          "The article reveals gender and case. Learn nominative plus genitive together. Plural γένη is nominative or accusative, while γενῶν is genitive plural. The same pattern explains ψύχους and θέρους in the reading."
        ],
