      {
        "title": "ἀρετή and κακία: abstract ideas as characters",
        "practiceTopic": "word-study",
        "body": [
          "ἀρετή can mean excellence or virtue; κακία can mean badness or vice. In an allegory, abstract terms become speakers. Capitalization in an English translation can signal that personification, but it does not turn the scene into history.",
          "Choose translations that fit the argument. “Excellence” can emphasize achievement; “virtue” can emphasize moral quality. Neither English word covers every Greek context by itself."
        ],
