        "title": "3. Numbers and measured claims",
        "practiceTopic": "numbers",
        "body": [
          "One, two, three, and four require special attention. εἷς/μία/ἕν has three genders; τρεῖς is masculine/feminine, τρία neuter; τέτταρες is masculine/feminine, τέτταρα neuter. Most cardinal numbers from five through one hundred are indeclinable.",
          "Numbers need not measure wisdom. The lesson’s inventory of books and resources is a teaching comparison, not a historical census of Euthydemus’s collection. Ordinals such as πρῶτος and δεύτερος decline as adjectives."
        ],
