        "id": "hos-family",
        "title": "4. ὡς and its compounds in context",
        "practiceTopic": "hos-family",
        "body": [
          "ὡς has several uses; let the sentence determine the sense. With a comparison it can mean “as”; with a superlative, “as ... as possible.” ὥσπερ means “just as,” and ὥστε commonly introduces a result, often with an infinitive.",
          "Do not force every ὡς into the English “that.” Here learn these reading patterns as units. Extended indirect statement and advanced clause systems belong to later lessons."
        ],
