        "title": "φυλάττω: protection and custody",
        "practiceTopic": "word-study",
        "body": [
          "φυλάττω can mean guard, watch, or protect. The English choice matters: guarding someone can provide security, restrict freedom, or both. Context supplies the relationship.",
          "ὁ φύλαξ names a guard; φυλάττεται can mean “is guarded.” Ask who holds power and whose interests the guarding serves. The word family helps trace actions without deciding their moral quality in advance."
        ],
