        "title": "Panthea is a person, not a test object",
        "body": [
          "Panthea’s position as a captive creates an unequal relationship with the man entrusted with guarding her. Her refusal and appeal for protection matter. Araspas’s responsibility does not pass to her because he experiences desire.",
          "Read the scene twice: first follow Araspas’s claims about himself; then follow Panthea’s choices within her constraints. What information becomes visible in the second reading? A lesson about self-mastery must also attend to the person exposed to another’s power."
        ]
      },
