        "title": "The passive can reveal or hide an actor",
        "body": [
          "“She is guarded” puts Panthea at the center of the sentence, but it can leave the guard unnamed. “She is guarded by Araspas” supplies the agent. Neither version by itself tells us whether that guard is trustworthy.",
          "Try rewriting a sentence about custody in active and passive forms. Keep the event the same, then explain which person each version foregrounds. Grammar changes emphasis; it does not erase responsibility."
        ]
