      {
        "title": "παιδεύω and πείθομαι",
        "practiceTopic": "word-study",
        "body": [
          "παιδεύω means educate or train; πείθομαι can mean obey or be persuaded. These meanings are related in this scene but are not identical. Being trained does not itself establish that someone has freely agreed.",
          "The passive ἐπαιδεύθη, “was educated,” names what happened to a person. Questions about purpose, authority, and consent require more than parsing that form."
        ],
