        "body": [
          "A supplementary participle completes a verb’s meaning rather than merely adding a circumstance. παύονται μαχόμενοι means “they stop fighting”; the participle agrees with the subject. With perception, ὁρᾷ τοὺς ἄνδρας ἀναβαίνοντας means “he sees the men going up”: the participle agrees with the accusative people perceived.",
          "Distinguish a supplementary participle from an attributive participle with an article and from a genitive absolute. Ask what the main verb needs: stop doing what? see whom doing what? Extended indirect discourse is reserved for later lessons."
