        "3. Participles that complete a verb: A supplementary participle completes a verb’s meaning rather than merely adding a circumstance. παύονται μαχόμενοι means “they stop fighting”; the participle agrees with the subject. With perception, ὁρᾷ τοὺς ἄνδρας ἀναβαίνοντας means “he sees the men going up”: the participle agrees with the accusative people perceived.",
